Wow...this one took a bit of work to finally force myself to finish.
It likely sat on NAO's servers for at least 2 months before I recently
got in the mood to finish it again.  The devnull tourney in November
really made me stop playing nethack for a bit of time, and well...these
conduct games just aren't as fun as free-for-all normal ones.  It takes
a bit of willpower to actually play the game a certain way.  I hope to
(in the near future) finish off my Illiterate valk game on NAO that I
started before the devnull tourney began.  She has the VS marked, an ac
of -10 or so, and some alchemy to do.  I just don't have any scrolls of
scare monster despite attempting to polypile all my blank scrolls.  I
might have a dunce cap, so that could be a last resort if i can't get
rid of a mind flayer via other means.  I'm sure I'll report on that one
at some point in the future.

This was one of my first games of a somewhat harder conduct, atheist.
It wasn't too bad as a deli handed me a potion of holy water early
game.  I saved this and used it as a seed for my holy water collection.
 I didn't have much gear until I ran across a bones pile at Juiblex.
Unfortunately, they died over water.  I ended up using scrolls of earth
(I didn't have a wand of cold with charges) and dug up the treasure.
Had the Helm of Brilliance (not important for the valk, but hey, it was
+4), GoP (also +4), and the +4 speed boots.  It also had a a bag of
holding, cursed of course, which I couldn't lift even after dropping
everything but holy water and my GoP which I was wearing.  I never
found a wand of cancellation but I did loot it on the way up with the
amulet.  It didn't really have much that I didn't already have so it
wasn't a big loss.

